2️⃣ Kubernetes Deployment Broke Production

Context

New deployment rolled out using CI/CD

Change involved config map / env var / image tag

Impact

Pods entered CrashLoopBackOff

Partial outage

Detection

Alert on pod restart count

Logs showed missing config / permission error

Action

Immediate rollback

Disabled pipeline auto-deploy

Used kubectl describe & logs

Resolution

Service restored within minutes

Learning

“We added canary deployments and mandatory config validation in CI. Rollbacks became automated instead of manual.”
___________________________________________________________________________--

Storytelling answer:

“In one incident, a new deployment was rolled out through our CI/CD pipeline. 
The change involved an update to a config map and environment variables.

Shortly after deployment, several pods started going into CrashLoopBackOff, leading to a partial outage.

We were alerted via a spike in pod restart counts, and when we checked the logs and kubectl describe,
it was clear that a required configuration value was missing, 
causing the application to fail on startup.

The immediate action was to roll back the deployment, which restored service quickly. To prevent further impact,
we temporarily disabled auto-deployments until 
we understood the root cause.

Once stable, we introduced canary deployments, added config validation as part of CI,
and automated rollback conditions.
